526:     //     * AW accepted at the upstream input until the upstream B handshake
527:     //       (covers the whole write, including completion AW/AR accepted by the
528:     //       output and held downstream, i.e. "accepted output pressure")
529:     //     * AR accepted until the upstream R-LAST handshake
530:     //     * W-LAST bursts accepted at the upstream input until the upstream B
531:     //       handshake.  A write is counted by its LAST beat and is NOT tracked
532:     //       by downstream forwarding: a write rejected by a bank (translation
533:     //       error) is consumed internally by that bank's error slave and
534:     //       answered with an upstream B, but it is NEVER forwarded to the
535:     //       completion port.  A forward-based W counter would therefore never
536:     //       decrement for those beats and in_flight_o would stay stuck high
537:     //       forever (phantom non-quiet).
538:     //     * w_partial_q: set when a W burst has started (a non-LAST beat was
539:     //       accepted upstream) and cleared when its LAST beat is accepted;
540:     //       covers the window between the first beat of a burst and its LAST.
541:     //     * both bank controller states (bank in_flight_o = state != IDLE)
542:     //   32-bit counters, asserted bounded / no underflow.  Increment and
543:     //   decrement on the same cycle are netted, so they can never produce a
544:     //   false underflow or a spurious overflow report.
